CORE
main.c
--function f --pointer-check
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A --function harness substitutes earlier arguments into a multidimensional
runtime static minimum and constructs an outer array satisfying that
precondition; this test deliberately makes no multidimensional access.
